  "configuration_id": "config_014",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_034 (RNA-only, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved the best result so far (acc=0.591, F1=0.573), substantially outperforming scgpt-based RNA-only (0.530) and all multimodal scgpt+resnet50 configs (0.512–0.525). This suggests the RNA encoder choice is the dominant factor, and image modality with scgpt actually hurt performance. Uncertainty: We have no data on whether image modality helps when paired with the stronger pca_n2000 encoder. Question tested: config_014 (multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is a single-variable extension of config_034—adding only the image branch with the simplest fusion (concat). This directly isolates whether image information provides any incremental value on top of the best RNA representation. Why this is the best next experiment: It is the most informative single test under budget constraints. If it exceeds 0.591, multimodal fusion with pca_n2000 is a promising direction to exploit. If it does not, we can confidently deprioritize multimodal configurations and focus remaining budget on RNA-only variants (e.g., transformer aggregation, singleprofile) or scvi_n200 encoders, avoiding costly exploration of a likely unproductive branch."
}

